WEBVTT

00:00:05.299 --> 00:00:10.550
<v Callum Reid>Morning, everyone. Can you hear me all right? Teams has picked the wrong microphone again.</v>

00:00:10.919 --> 00:00:18.620
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, you're there. Honestly, the traffic on the ring road this morning. I spent longer looking at the same van than driving.</v>

00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:25.289
<v David Whitfield>Lovely way to start a Friday. Bit of quality time with a diesel Transit.</v>

00:00:26.469 --> 00:00:32.420
<v Jamie Brennan>And whose new car's in the car park? Very shiny. Brave, parking it next to that puddle.</v>

00:00:32.969 --> 00:00:36.469
<v Aisha Begum>Not mine. Mine's the one where the dirt is structural.</v>

00:00:37.759 --> 00:00:44.060
<v Callum Reid>Right, Friday the 23rd of January. Let's do the closed stuff first, then what's actually ours to do.</v>

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:52.670
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah so, I finished the repair on the main conveyor last night. That's done, not something I'm carrying into today.</v>

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:59.719
<v Callum Reid>Good. Repair closed, then. There is a separate contractor booking on the list, but we're not reopening your repair.</v>

00:01:01.119 --> 00:01:07.420
<v Priya Raman>And I already swapped the filter on the palletiser yesterday. That old entry can stop haunting the conversation.</v>

00:01:09.579 --> 00:01:12.379
<v David Whitfield>Those entries live longer than the filters, usually.</v>

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:20.689
<v Hannah Price>While we're clearing those, I signed off the inspection on the Injection Moulding Line 2 on Tuesday. All finished.</v>

00:01:21.049 --> 00:01:23.849
<v Callum Reid>Yep, those are completed items, not fresh jobs.</v>

00:01:24.590 --> 00:01:31.590
<v Aisha Begum>Only an observation from me: noticed the turbine two was running a bit warm on nights, but it settled down.</v>

00:01:32.689 --> 00:01:36.189
<v Callum Reid>Settled back down, yeah? You're not raising another job there?</v>

00:01:37.079 --> 00:01:41.629
<v Aisha Begum>No, just passing on what I saw. Nothing new for today off that.</v>

00:01:43.590 --> 00:01:52.689
<v Priya Raman>Same sort of thing, separately — noticed the Line 1 Hydraulic Power Unit was running a bit warm on nights, but it settled down. Observation only.</v>

00:01:54.230 --> 00:01:58.079
<v Callum Reid>Understood. Neither of those is going on as a new action.</v>

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:04.950
<v David Whitfield>And the supplier still hasn't confirmed the delivery for the GT2. That's still blocked, before anyone asks.</v>

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:11.009
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, there's no confirmed delivery date. Nothing firmer than what we had.</v>

00:02:11.490 --> 00:02:15.689
<v Callum Reid>Right, existing blocker. Not inventing a new delivery job out of it.</v>

00:02:17.430 --> 00:02:21.979
<v Callum Reid>Davey, can you swap the filter on the dryer? Normal priority, that one.</v>

00:02:23.129 --> 00:02:26.979
<v David Whitfield>Yeah. Routine filter swap, not suddenly the top of the pile?</v>

00:02:28.479 --> 00:02:29.680
<v Callum Reid>Exactly. Normal priority.</v>

00:02:30.590 --> 00:02:34.090
<v David Whitfield>Fine, I'll swap the filter on the dryer. That's mine.</v>

00:02:35.509 --> 00:02:43.909
<v Callum Reid>Fiona, can you investigate the pressure drop on the Water Booster Pump by the end of the week? It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:51.199
<v Fiona Doyle>Um, yes — investigation, though, rather than me committing to having a repair finished?</v>

00:02:51.639 --> 00:02:54.439
<v Callum Reid>Yes, investigate the pressure drop. That's the action.</v>

00:02:56.280 --> 00:03:02.229
<v Fiona Doyle>Okay, I'll investigate the pressure drop on the Water Booster Pump by the end of the week.</v>

00:03:03.389 --> 00:03:08.639
<v Callum Reid>I know it's Friday already. Still matters, but don't treat that as a drop-everything one.</v>

00:03:10.469 --> 00:03:11.870
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, understood. That's clear.</v>

00:03:13.819 --> 00:03:20.120
<v Callum Reid>Aisha, can you do a site visit at Kestrel with the contractor today, whenever you get a chance?</v>

00:03:20.710 --> 00:03:24.909
<v Aisha Begum>Yep, I'll do the site visit at Kestrel with the contractor today.</v>

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:30.319
<v Callum Reid>No particular slot from me. Whenever you get a chance, just within today.</v>

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:34.710
<v Aisha Begum>That's fine. Gives me a bit of breathing room.</v>

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:42.530
<v Callum Reid>Han, can you book a contractor to look at the main conveyor on the 3rd? Low priority.</v>

00:03:43.349 --> 00:03:50.349
<v Hannah Price>Sorry, on the 3rd is when I make the booking, rather than you saying the contractor has to attend then?</v>

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:57.469
<v Callum Reid>Yes, the booking action on the 3rd. Low priority; I'm not setting an attendance date here.</v>

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:04.490
<v Hannah Price>Right, I'll book a contractor to look at the main conveyor on the 3rd.</v>

00:04:04.819 --> 00:04:11.469
<v Fiona Doyle>And that's separate from the repair I finished last night, just so those don't get mashed into one line.</v>

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:17.750
<v Callum Reid>Exactly. Finished repair stays finished. This is just that contractor booking.</v>

00:04:18.959 --> 00:04:27.009
<v Priya Raman>I've got the bearing one. I'll take vibration readings on the GT2 Number 2 Bearing by 11am. I'll drop everything for that one.</v>

00:04:27.769 --> 00:04:33.370
<v Callum Reid>Thanks, Priya Raman. Yes, drop everything for that one — by 11am is the important bit.</v>

00:04:35.569 --> 00:04:38.019
<v Priya Raman>Yep. I'm taking it, readings by 11am.</v>

00:04:38.389 --> 00:04:43.290
<v David Whitfield>Sorry, was talking over you there. Heard it now — that's the urgent one.</v>

00:04:44.639 --> 00:04:51.639
<v Callum Reid>Fiona, the other one for you: can you run a function test on the air dryer by Wednesday? Fairly important.</v>

00:04:52.490 --> 00:04:57.389
<v Fiona Doyle>By Wednesday, yep. I've got that as a function test, not the filter swap.</v>

00:04:59.509 --> 00:05:04.410
<v Callum Reid>Correct. Fairly important, but it's not in the same category as those vibration readings.</v>

00:05:05.339 --> 00:05:09.540
<v Fiona Doyle>Okay, I'll run a function test on the air dryer by Wednesday.</v>

00:05:10.930 --> 00:05:15.829
<v Callum Reid>Jamie, can you run the monthly fire alarm test today at 2pm? Normal priority.</v>

00:05:16.350 --> 00:05:22.649
<v Jamie Brennan>Yep, I'll run the monthly fire alarm test today at 2pm. Normal priority, fixed time — got it.</v>

00:05:24.139 --> 00:05:27.639
<v Hannah Price>Two this afternoon, not part of this morning's noise, then.</v>

00:05:29.949 --> 00:05:34.500
<v Jamie Brennan>Correct. My microphone is the only alarm you're getting from me this morning.</v>

00:05:35.720 --> 00:05:43.769
<v Callum Reid>Fiona, can you write up the near miss at the Line 2 Safety Guard Interlock this afternoon? It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:05:46.139 --> 00:05:53.839
<v Fiona Doyle>I can't take that as well, sorry. With the Water Booster Pump investigation, I haven't got room for the write-up this afternoon.</v>

00:05:55.439 --> 00:06:03.490
<v Callum Reid>Fair enough. Hannah, can you take that instead — write up the near miss at the Line 2 Safety Guard Interlock this afternoon?</v>

00:06:04.189 --> 00:06:11.889
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, I'll take it instead of Fiona. I'll write up the near miss at the Line 2 Safety Guard Interlock this afternoon.</v>

00:06:13.639 --> 00:06:18.889
<v Fiona Doyle>Thanks. Just to be clear, that's off me, not both of us down for it.</v>

00:06:19.620 --> 00:06:25.569
<v Callum Reid>Yes, Hannah owns that now. It matters but it's not urgent; this afternoon is still the deadline.</v>

00:06:27.329 --> 00:06:28.730
<v Hannah Price>Understood. Mine, this afternoon.</v>

00:06:30.689 --> 00:06:39.790
<v Callum Reid>One still needing an owner: do the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the GT2 Inlet Water Injection Valve first thing tomorrow. That one's safety critical, straight away.</v>

00:06:41.949 --> 00:06:46.149
<v David Whitfield>I can't take that one. Don't put my name against the sign-off.</v>

00:06:48.589 --> 00:06:51.740
<v Priya Raman>I can't commit to first thing tomorrow either. Sorry.</v>

00:06:52.230 --> 00:06:58.529
<v Callum Reid>Anyone else able to take that exact sign-off? First thing tomorrow, safety critical — not something to drift.</v>

00:06:59.860 --> 00:07:02.660
<v Aisha Begum>Not me, I'm afraid. I can't accept it.</v>

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:07.600
<v Jamie Brennan>Nor me. I'm not taking ownership of that.</v>

00:07:09.129 --> 00:07:18.579
<v Callum Reid>Right, nobody has taken the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the GT2 Inlet Water Injection Valve. It remains unallocated, not signed off or agreed safe by this meeting.</v>

00:07:20.410 --> 00:07:23.910
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, leave it visibly unallocated. Silence isn't someone accepting it.</v>

00:07:24.310 --> 00:07:30.259
<v Callum Reid>Exactly. And Priya Raman, your GT2 Number 2 Bearing readings are still the drop-everything item, by 11am.</v>

00:07:32.310 --> 00:07:35.110
<v Priya Raman>Yes, I'll have those readings taken by 11am.</v>

00:07:35.649 --> 00:07:39.149
<v Callum Reid>Right. That's where we are, including the gap. Cheers, everyone.</v>
